  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-carbonate-system-definitions",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-carbonate-system-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "21e66b2c314b75cf7dc1686ccf50982ccd163493b1761b789634d05c433243bd",
      "reason": "Defines dissic, talk and ph (total scale) and what talk includes, which is needed to compare them with GLODAP TCO2, TAlk and pH.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compare model `ph` (total scale) only with GLODAP's in-situ total-scale pH `pHtsinsitutp`, not `pHts25p0`, which is a different quantity. Derived fields cover the whole water column.",
        "`dissic` and `talk` are per volume (mol m-3); convert to µmol kg-1 before comparing with GLODAP. State that the CESM2 carbonate constants are undocumented (unverified assumption), and that the models differ in their alkalinity terms (MPI-ESM1.2 added phosphate and silicate alkalinity)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "Model dissic and talk are stored in mol m-3 while GLODAP is per unit mass, so a conversion to µmol kg-1 is needed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ with the in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`), not a fixed-pressure sigma. The `transform_unit` default is a constant surface density and errs by about 1 % at depth. State the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`). Multiplying mol m-3 by 1000 and calling it µmol/kg is wrong.",
        "The 2002 minus 1971-2000 change in DIC is a difference between two periods on the model's own basis; if the density-converted values are used, convert both periods with the same treatment. `ph` (unitless) needs no conversion."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The map bias, RMSE and correlation, the depth-profile bias and the Figure 1 maps all need one common mask on the GLODAP grid, covering all fields and models.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GLODAP is the reference, not WOA23, so build the mask with `build_comparison_mask(..., ocean_only=False)`. The WOA23 coastline would drop GLODAP cells and flatter the models.",
        "Build ONE mask across all three models and GLODAP for the 0-50 m DIC map metrics, applied with `.where(mask)`, and report the cell counts. At each depth (0, 100, 500, 1000, 2000 m) take the cells from the fields at that depth, because coverage shrinks with depth. The question asks for the cells where each model and GLODAP are both defined, so use a per-model mask at each depth. Report `mean_data`, `mean_reference` and the bias from `compute_difference_metrics` over the same sample."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The global 0-50 m means must be volume-weighted over all cells, using each model's own areacello and volcello.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 0-50 m global means (one mean over all of a source's 0-50 m cells) are volume-weighted: `compute_basic_stat` with `op='volume_weighted_mean'`, with weights masked to the valid cells. Use the model's `volcello`; for GLODAP use the layer thicknesses over the same valid cells. Plain `mean` is wrong.",
        "For map metrics use area weighting: `compute_difference_metrics` (area by default) and `analyze_correlation` with `weighting='area'` for the spatial correlation. The depth-wise global mean bias is also area-weighted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The areacello and volcello weights are extensive tracer-cell fields, and layer thickness can be recovered as volcello/areacello for the 0-50 m averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Layer thickness = `volcello` / `areacello`, not the `lev_bnds` difference (GFDL-ESM4 differs by 14 % of cells, MPI partial cells by up to ±50 %). The 0-50 m weights must respect partial cells. State the `attrs['area_source']` and `attrs['volume_source']` used.",
        "The models' ocean areas differ by about a per cent; do not rescale them, and state which area each integral covers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Global means should be computed on the native grid, with regridding only for the maps and the pattern comparison on the GLODAP 1° grid.",
      "status": "dropped",
      "notes": [
        "The global means (first, second and fifth items) and the period change are numbers: compute them on each source's native grid with its own weights. Regrid to the GLODAP 1° grid (`regrid_horizontal`, 'conservative', state the method) only for the map bias, RMSE and correlation and for the depth-profile comparison.",
        "For 0, 100, 500, 1000 and 2000 m, interpolate each product to those depths with `regrid_vertical` rather than selecting the nearest level. The 0-50 m map is each cell's mean over its own 0-50 m levels, integrated on the original levels before regridding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The 2002 minus 1971-2000 change is an anomaly relative to a defined baseline period, and its ratio to the GLODAP bias shows how much of the bias is a time offset.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The period change, 2002 minus the 1971-2000 average, is an anomaly against the model's own climatology. State this baseline. The model bias is not removed by it, so compare the change with the offset from GLODAP to judge whether the offset is a model error or a period or drift effect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Land and below-sea-floor cells carry the 1e20 missing value, which would silently dominate the sums and means if left unmasked.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use NaN-aware reductions with the weights masked to the same valid cells. Build each field's mask from the field itself (`dissic`, `talk`, `ph` can differ). A value near 1e20 in the output is an unmasked fill value."
